## Responsibilities of Each Layer

### ice-telemetry: Observability Foundation

The bottom layer is `ice-telemetry`, which defines span and event contracts. The default implementation is noop, meaning if you don't need telemetry, there's zero overhead.

```rust
// Core trait in ice-telemetry
pub trait TelemetrySpan {
    fn record<K: Into<Str>, V: Into<Value>>(&mut self, key: K, value: V);
    fn event<E: Into<Event>>(&mut self, event: E);
}
```

### ice-ai: Unified LLM Abstraction

`ice-ai` is where things get interesting. It defines unified types like `Message`, `Provider`, `AssistantMessageEvent`, allowing upper-layer code to never care whether the backend is Anthropic, OpenAI, or your own service.

```rust
// Provider trait - the only LLM boundary
pub trait Provider: Send + Sync + 'static {
    fn stream(
        &self,
        model: &Model,
        context: Context,
        options: Option<SimpleStreamOptions>,
    ) -> Pin<Box<dyn Future<Output = Result<AssistantMessageEventStream, AiError>>>>;
}
```

